 runs 75 years, 1951 to 2025, on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids. January to February came in under 90% of normal in 36 of those years, more than any other pair. In 2025 August to September came in at 48% of normal, and in 2026 so far March to April sits at 204% of normal. Every grid had its driest year in 1963, with grid 26581 at 60% of normal.</p>"}
